  <div class="case-label">Case 001</div>
  <h1 class="case-title">Omjine — Precious One</h1>
  <p class="case-sub">A full release campaign built from scratch in two weeks.</p>

  <div class="meta-grid">
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Artist</div><div class="meta-val">Omjine</div></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Location</div><div class="meta-val">Seoul, South Korea</div></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Release date</div><div class="meta-val">10 April 2026</div></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Lead time</div><div class="meta-val">2 weeks</div></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Sound</div><div class="meta-val">Cat Power, The xx</div></div>
    <div class="meta-item"><div class="meta-key">Fee</div><div class="meta-val">Pro bono</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>The Artist</h2>
  <p>Omjine is the project of Eomjin Cho, a singer-songwriter born in Chuncheon, South Korea and raised in Selangor, Malaysia. She has been writing and recording her own music since her teens and started experimenting with home production in 2008. Her debut EP Big Hearts came out in 2021, followed by the single Bus Driver in 2023.</p>
  <p>She came to Ardito ahead of her third release with a clear artistic identity but no campaign infrastructure in place: no press contacts, no outreach system, no mailing list, and no experience pitching to media.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <h2>The Brief</h2>
  <p>Precious One is Omjine's debut single under Ardito's management. It is written from the perspective of the antagonist in someone else's story, imagining what they would want to say back after everything had already been told. The production is sparse and home recorded, built around a strong vocal and a rhythm that keeps pulling forward.</p>
  <p>Ardito took this campaign on without a fee. The brief came in two weeks before release date, so consider this a stress test of what's possible with a tight window and no runway.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <h2>What Ardito Did</h2>

  <p>The first thing that needed fixing was not the pitching. Omjine had never registered with a collecting society, which meant every radio play she had ever received had earned her nothing in performance royalties. She registered with KOMCA before the campaign started and backdated her catalogue. That one conversation was probably the most valuable thing that happened.</p>

  <p>From there: 62 contacts imported from DistroKid into Mailchimp, two email campaigns written in her voice, a pre-save and a release day send. Distribution submitted with ISRC and UPC filed. Spotify for Artists editorial pitch submitted. Platform access set up across Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube, and DistroKid. Content planned around what she was actually comfortable making rather than what looked good on paper.</p>

  <p>Fifteen pitch emails went out to blogs and radio stations on the Tuesday morning before release. Each one was written for the specific publication, not adapted from a template. Blogs got a private SoundCloud link. Radio got the MP3 attached directly.</p>

  <div class="contacts-list">
    <span class="contact-tag">The Line of Best Fit</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Atwood Magazine</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Obscure Sound</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">A&R Factory</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">GoldFlakePaint</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">KLOF Mag</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">For The Love Of Bands</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Beats Per Minute</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">BBC Introducing</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Radio Fandango</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Denmark Street Radio</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Soho Radio</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">Amazing Radio</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">WFUV</span>
    <span class="contact-tag">KEXP</span>
  </div>

  <p>SubmitHub was used on the free tier with Advanced Mode enabled. Genre tags were corrected before submission so the track reached relevant curators. Post-release submissions to Soundplate, BIRP, Indiemono, and Pitchplaylists were queued once the track was confirmed live on Spotify.</p>

  <div class="divider"></div>

